        "modal_content": "<p><em><strong>Igni</strong></em><strong>ton</strong>  technology was originally developed in the 90’s, and in 1995 the lab was created in Switzerland with much of the hardware to verify and measure ignitons being rented from CERN. The current lab is located in Colorado.</p><p>The component stages of the <em>Igni</em>ton characterization system are from the Swiss laboratories, that were used until 2023.  After collecting more data on the nature of the quasi-particles and their industrial applications,  the current equipment was designed and constructed in Colorado.</p><p>Ignitons, as neutral quasi-particles like neutrinos, have no electrical charge and are extremely small.  Known as Life-Force or World Spirit in ancient Egypt, <em>Igni</em>tons gave life to the original prokaryote bacteria on Earth which gained life from their ability to attract and retain ignitons.</p><p><em>Igni</em>ton technology creates a quantum interaction between protons and ignitons which allows ignitons to disperse geometrically on the proton’s peripheral gray region to improve quantum energy and efficacy of targeted molecules.</p><p>University studies published in peer-reviewed medical journals show significant improvement of memory, attention and other cognitive functions.</p>",
