      "blocks": {
        "ingredient_bGdfcq": {
          "type": "ingredient",
          "settings": {
            "ingredient_name": "Citicoline",
            "ingredient_tagline": "THE BRAIN ENERGIZER**",
            "ingredient_description": "<p>Citicoline is a potent nootropic compound that supports the production of acetylcholine, a neurotransmitter essential for memory, attention, and cognitive function. It also aids in neuron membrane support and promotes mental energy, making it ideal for anyone seeking better focus and brain performance.**</p>",
            "benefits_list": "Mitochondrial Health**\nMemory Support**\nFocus & Attention**\nMental Energy**\nNeuroprotective Support**\nBrain Cell Health**",
            "ingredient_image": "shopify://shop_images/igniton-cognition-citicoline_1.avif",
            "quantum_enhancement": "Supports brain cell membranes and memory.**",
            "anchor_id": "quantum-ingredient",
            "extended_description": "<p>Citicoline (CDP-choline) is a naturally occurring compound that serves as a precursor to both choline and cytidine, making it uniquely effective for brain health. Research shows it enhances multiple neurotransmitter systems while supporting cellular membrane integrity.**</p>",
            "how_it_works": "<p>Citicoline (CDP-choline) works by supplying the brain with choline and cytidine, two key molecules involved in the synthesis of phospholipids and neurotransmitters. Choline is essential for the production of acetylcholine, a neurotransmitter that regulates memory and attention, while cytidine is converted into uridine, which supports the synthesis of neuronal membranes. This dual-action mechanism helps reinforce brain cell integrity, enhance communication between neurons, and support healthy cognitive performance, especially in areas like focus, mental energy, and learning.**</p>",
            "formulation_synergy": "<p>Citicoline synergizes with the other ingredients in <em>IgniCognition™ </em>by supporting the amplification of the brain's cholinergic system while enhancing the structural and energetic integrity of neurons.**</p><p>As a precursor to acetylcholine, Citicoline directly supports memory, focus, and mental processing, complementing Alpha-GPC’s choline donation and Phosphatidylserine’s role in membrane fluidity.**</p><p>When paired with NADH and CoQ10—both critical for mitochondrial energy—Citicoline ensures that the cognitive pathways it activates are well-fueled.** </p><p>This synergistic blend, especially when quantum-enhanced with Ignitons, supports comprehensive neurocognitive performance across neurotransmitter, membrane, and metabolic systems.**</p>",
            "research_highlights": "Clinically shown to support strong memory and attention, particularly in older adults**\nEnhances acetylcholine production, supporting neurotransmission critical for learning and mental clarity**\nSupports brain cell membrane repair and synthesis, aiding neuroplasticity and neuronal health**\nDemonstrated neuroprotective support in conditions involving ischemia and neurodegeneration**\nSupports brain energy metabolism, especially in regions linked to cognition (as shown in imaging studies)**",
            "dosage_info": "",
            "safety_notes": "Clinically studied for cognitive support and brain metabolism**\nNaturally occurring compound with excellent safety profile**\nGRAS status recognized in the U.S.\nThird-party tested for purity and potency"
          }
        },
        "ingredient_e8wdAC": {
          "type": "ingredient",
          "settings": {
            "ingredient_name": "Alpha-GPC",
            "ingredient_tagline": "THE COGNITIVE CATALYST**",
            "ingredient_description": "<p>Alpha-GPC is an absorbable form of choline that delivers support for cognitive health, mental sharpness, and neuroplasticity. It's known to boost growth hormone and improve synaptic signaling, which supports strong short- and long-term memory.**</p>",
            "benefits_list": "Mitochondrial Health**\nAcetylcholine Elevation**\nNeuroplasticity Support**\nGrowth Hormone Release**\nCognitive Processing Speed**",
            "ingredient_image": "shopify://shop_images/igniton-cognition-alpha-gpc_1.webp",
            "quantum_enhancement": "Supports mitochondrial uptake and ATP production**",
            "anchor_id": "quantum-ingredient",
            "extended_description": "<p>Alpha-GPC (L-Alpha glycerylphosphorylcholine) is considered the gold standard of choline supplements and one of the most bioavailable sources available. It's a natural compound found in small amounts in the brain and in foods like dairy, organ meats, and wheat germ. Unlike other choline sources, Alpha-GPC is both water-soluble and lipid-soluble, allowing maximum efficiency.**</p><p>What makes Alpha-GPC special is its structure: it's choline bound to a glycerophosphate group, which not only supports absorption but also provides additional benefits supporting cell membrane health. When Alpha-GPC reaches the brain, it rapidly increases acetylcholine levels while also contributing to phospholipid synthesis—supporting both neurotransmitter function and brain cell structure.**</p><p>Alpha-GPC is used by elite athletes for cognitive performance, by students for studying and test-taking, and by older adults for memory support. It's one of the few nootropics that has demonstrated benefits across all age groups, from young adults to elderly populations.**</p>",
            "how_it_works": "<p>Alpha-GPC works through several powerful mechanisms:</p><p><strong>Acetylcholine Elevation:</strong> Alpha-GPC is an effective supplement for supporting brain acetylcholine levels. Studies show it may increase brain choline levels by up to 45% within hours of ingestion. This supports strong focus, memory formation, and recall speed.**</p><p><strong>Neuroplasticity Support:</strong> By supporting acetylcholine and providing phospholipids for membrane health, Alpha-GPC supports the brain's ability to form new neural connections—the basis of learning and memory. This is particularly valuable for learning new skills or retaining complex information.**</p><p><strong>Growth Hormone Release:</strong> Unique among choline compounds, Alpha-GPC has been shown to support growth hormone release from the pituitary gland. This contributes to muscle recovery, body composition, and healthy-aging effects.**</p><p><strong>Cognitive Processing Speed:</strong> Research shows Alpha-GPC supports the speed of cognitive tasks, reaction time, and mental agility—making it valuable for situations requiring quick thinking and rapid decision-making.**</p><p><strong>Neuroprotection Support:</strong> Alpha-GPC has been studied for supporting strong cognitive health, brain recovery, and maintaining cognitive function during aging.**</p>",
            "formulation_synergy": "<p>Works synergistically with Resveratrol to activate longevity pathways. When combined with PQQ, it creates a powerful mitochondrial support system that supports energy production at the cellular level.**</p>",
            "research_highlights": "Clinical studies show strong memory and attention in healthy adults within 90 minutes**\nMeta-analysis confirms benefits for supporting healthy age-related cognition**\nResearch demonstrates 45% increase in brain choline levels after supplementation**\nStudies show strong power output and growth hormone response in athletes**\nUsed clinically in Europe for cognitive strength with proven efficacy**\nOver 40 clinical trials supporting safety and effectiveness**",
            "dosage_info": "",
            "safety_notes": "Shown to support acetylcholine levels and brain function**\nWell-tolerated in clinical trials at standard doses**\nThird-party tested for contaminants and purity"
          }
        },
        "ingredient_9hCJFK": {
          "type": "ingredient",
          "settings": {
            "ingredient_name": "N-Acetyl L-Tyrosine",
            "ingredient_tagline": "THE FOCUS ENHANCER**",
            "ingredient_description": "<p>N-Acetyl L-Tyrosine (NALT) is a bioavailable form of L-Tyrosine that fuels the production of dopamine, norepinephrine, and epinephrine—neurotransmitters that help you stay focused, motivated, and calm under occasional stress. Perfect for peak mental performance in high-pressure situations.**</p>",
            "benefits_list": "Mitochondrial Health**\nFocus & Concentration**\nStress Resilience**\nMental Clarity**\nMotivation Support**",
            "ingredient_image": "shopify://shop_images/igniton-cognition-n-acetyl-l-tyrosine.webp",
            "quantum_enhancement": "Energizes cells, supports cognitive clarity**",
            "anchor_id": "quantum-ingredient",
            "extended_description": "<p>N-Acetyl L-Tyrosine (NALT) is an acetylated derivative of L-Tyrosine, designed for improved solubility and bioavailability, making it more efficient for supplementation—especially under occasional stress.**</p><p>As a key precursor in the synthesis of catecholamine neurotransmitters—dopamine, norepinephrine, and epinephrine—NALT plays a vital role in regulating mood, motivation, alertness, and the body’s response to occasional stress.** </p><p>During periods of high cognitive demand or emotional strain, these neurotransmitters can become depleted, leading to fatigue, mental fog, and diminished performance. By providing a direct and efficient supply of tyrosine, NALT helps sustain optimal neurotransmitter levels, supporting both mental clarity and emotional balance.**</p>",
            "how_it_works": "<p>N-Acetyl L-Tyrosine (NALT) is a highly bioavailable form of the amino acid L-Tyrosine, which serves as a precursor to the catecholamine neurotransmitters—dopamine, norepinephrine, and epinephrine. </p><p>These neurotransmitters are essential for maintaining focus, motivation, mood, and resilience to occasional stress, particularly during mentally demanding or high-pressure situations.**</p><p>By supporting neurotransmitter synthesis, especially under conditions where these chemicals may be depleted (such as occasional stress, fatigue, or cognitive overload), NALT helps maintain mental clarity, enhance cognitive flexibility, and promote a balanced emotional state.**</p><p>Its acetylated form increases solubility and absorption compared to standard L-Tyrosine, making it a preferred choice for nootropic and performance-focused formulations.**</p>",
            "formulation_synergy": "<p>N-Acetyl L-Tyrosine (NALT) works synergistically within the <em>IgniCognition™</em> formula by complementing both the neurotransmitter and energy-support pathways of the brain.**</p><p>When combined with Citicoline and Alpha-GPC, which support cholinergic function, NALT helps balance catecholaminergic and cholinergic signaling for strong focus, attention, and emotional regulation.**</p><p>Its synergy extends further with NADH and CoQ10, both of which support mitochondrial energy production. Since neurotransmitter synthesis is energy-dependent, NALT’s function is amplified by the increased cellular vitality these ingredients provide.**</p><p>This alignment between neurotransmitter production and energy supply, especially when enhanced with Igniton-charged biofield coherence, helps deliver consistent, high-performance cognitive support across demanding mental environments.**</p>",
            "research_highlights": "Supports dopamine and norepinephrine synthesis, critical for focus, motivation, and mood regulation**\nShown to support cognitive performance under stress, including during sleep deprivation and high-pressure tasks**\nMore bioavailable than standard L-Tyrosine, especially in water-soluble forms, making it ideal for supplementation**\nMay reduce cognitive fatigue during multitasking or prolonged mental work**\nUsed in military and cognitive resilience research for its role in sustaining performance under duress**",
            "dosage_info": "",
            "safety_notes": "No serious side effects reported at recommended dosages\nThird-party tested for contaminants and purity"
          }
        },
        "ingredient_RpNTMr": {
          "type": "ingredient",
          "settings": {
            "ingredient_name": "Phosphatidylserine",
            "ingredient_tagline": "THE MENTAL OPTIMIZER**",
            "ingredient_description": "<p>Phosphatidylserine is a phospholipid critical for healthy brain cell membranes and neurotransmitter function. It boosts memory and supports enhanced mental processing speed and healthy cortisol levels, helping you stay sharp and balanced.**<br/><br/></p>",
            "benefits_list": "Mitochondrial Health**\nMemory Support**\nImproved Focus**\nMental Energy**\nNeuroprotection Support**",
            "ingredient_image": "shopify://shop_images/igniton-cognition-phosphatidylserine.webp",
            "quantum_enhancement": "Supports brain cell membranes and memory.**",
            "anchor_id": "quantum-ingredient",
            "extended_description": "<p>Phosphatidylserine (PS) is a phospholipid—a type of fat molecule—that's a critical structural component of cell membranes throughout the body, with the highest concentrations found in brain tissue. It makes up about 15% of the brain's phospholipid content and is particularly enriched in neuronal membranes, where it plays essential roles in cell signaling, neurotransmitter release, and cognitive function.**</p><p>While your body can produce phosphatidylserine, levels naturally decline with age, and synthesis may not keep pace with demand during periods of occasional stress or cognitive challenge. Supplementation has been shown to support optimal levels and support cognitive performance across multiple domains.**</p><p>Phosphatidylserine is one of the few brain health supplements with FDA-qualified health claims, and it's been the subject of numerous clinical trials demonstrating support for strong memory, cognitive processing, and occasional stress response. It's particularly valued for its dual benefits: cognitive support and occasional stress modulation.**</p>",
            "how_it_works": "<p>Phosphatidylserine (PS) works by supporting the structure and fluidity of brain cell membranes, which are essential for effective cell signaling and neurotransmitter release.**</p><p>As a naturally occurring phospholipid concentrated in neuronal membranes, PS plays a key role in enabling neurons to communicate efficiently, process information, and respond to stimuli. This makes it foundational to memory formation, learning, and overall cognitive performance.**</p><p>Additionally, PS helps modulate cortisol—the body’s primary stress hormone—particularly during times of occasional mental or physical stress.**</p><p>This contributes to its reputation not only as a cognitive enhancer but also as a support for emotional balance and resilience. **</p><p>Healthy PS levels support both brain function and a healthy stress response.**</p>",
            "formulation_synergy": "<p>Phosphatidylserine (PS) synergizes with the other ingredients in <em>IgniCognition™</em> by supporting neuronal membrane fluidity, which optimizes the function of neurotransmitters like acetylcholine and dopamine—both of which are supported by Citicoline, Alpha-GPC, and N-Acetyl L-Tyrosine.**</p><p>By creating a stable, responsive environment for neurotransmission, PS allows these compounds to work more efficiently, supporting sharp memory, fast processing, and strong focus.**</p><p>This synergy extends to NADH and CoQ10, which power the mitochondria to fuel cognitive processes. PS ensures that this energy is delivered to cells functioning at their structural best.**</p><p>In high-demand mental environments, this harmony between membrane integrity, neurotransmitter availability, and cellular energy enables sustained clarity, resilience, and performance.**</p>",
            "research_highlights": "Over 3,000 published studies on phosphatidylserine and brain health**\nClinical trials show 20-30% improvement in memory scores after 12 weeks**\nResearch demonstrates healthy cortisol response to occasional stress**\nFDA-qualified health claim for reducing risk of cognitive decline**\nStudies show improved golf performance and cognitive function in athletes**\nMeta-analysis confirms benefits across multiple cognitive domains**",
            "dosage_info": "",
            "safety_notes": "FDA-qualified health claim for age-related cognitive decline**\nExtensively studied and considered safe for long-term use\nThird-party tested for contaminants and purity"
          }
        },
        "ingredient_HpmBWW": {
          "type": "ingredient",
          "settings": {
            "ingredient_name": "CoQ10",
            "ingredient_tagline": "THE CELLULAR ENERGIZER**",
            "ingredient_description": "<p>Coenzyme Q10 plays a key role in the production of ATP (energy) at the cellular level. With antioxidant properties, CoQ10 helps support your brain and heart against occasional oxidative stress, while supporting mitochondrial health and long-term vitality.**<br/><br/></p>",
            "benefits_list": "Mitochondrial Health**\nCellular Energy Support**\nAntioxidant Properties**\nMental Energy**\nCardiovascular Support**\nNeuroprotection Support**",
            "ingredient_image": "shopify://shop_images/igniton-cognition-coq10_1.jpg",
            "quantum_enhancement": "Supports mitochondrial uptake and ATP production**",
            "anchor_id": "quantum-ingredient",
            "extended_description": "<p>Coenzyme Q10 (CoQ10), also known as ubiquinone, is a naturally occurring compound found in virtually every cell of your body, with the highest concentrations in organs with high energy demands: the heart, brain, liver, and kidneys. It's an essential component of the electron transport chain in mitochondria, where it plays a critical role in ATP (cellular energy) production.**</p><p>CoQ10 also functions with powerful fat-soluble antioxidant properties, supporting cell membranes and other lipid structures from occasional oxidative stress. CoQ10 levels naturally decline with age—by age 40, levels can be 30% lower than in youth, and by age 70, they may be 50-60% lower; resulting in reduced energy, cognition, and increased oxidative stress.**</p><p>While your body can synthesize CoQ10, production requires eight vitamins and multiple enzymatic steps—a process that becomes less efficient with aging. Supplementation has been shown to support healthy levels and support energy production, particularly in tissues with high metabolic demands like the brain.**</p>",
            "how_it_works": "<p>CoQ10 works through two primary mechanisms:</p><p>ATP Production: CoQ10 is an essential cofactor in the electron transport chain—the series of reactions in mitochondria that produces ATP, your cells' energy currency. It shuttles electrons between Complex I/II and Complex III, facilitating the production of up to 95% of your body's energy. Without adequate CoQ10, ATP production declines, leading to fatigue and reduced cellular function.**</p><p>In the brain, where neurons have extraordinarily high energy demands (the brain uses 20% of your body's energy despite being only 2% of body weight), CoQ10 is critical for maintaining optimal cognitive function. Healthy mitochondrial function translates to healthy mental energy, processing speed, and sustained focus.**</p><p>Antioxidant Properties: CoQ10 has antioxidant properties that work within mitochondrial membranes, supporting them from occasional oxidative stress generated during ATP production. It also helps support other antioxidant properties like vitamin E, extending their supporting effects.**</p><p>This dual role—energy production and antioxidant properties—makes CoQ10 uniquely valuable for supporting long-term brain health and cognitive performance.**</p><p>Cardiovascular Support: CoQ10 is highly concentrated in heart tissue and supports cardiovascular function, blood pressure regulation, and endothelial health—all of which affect brain perfusion and cognitive performance.**</p>",
            "formulation_synergy": "<p>CoQ10 creates powerful synergies throughout <em>Igni</em>Cognition. It works closely with NADH as both are critical components of the electron transport chain. NADH donates electrons at Complex I, which are then passed through CoQ10 at Complex III—working together, they ensure maximum ATP production efficiency.**</p><p>The combination with all the nootropics in the formula is essential: optimal neural activity (from enhanced neurotransmitter signaling via Citicoline, Alpha-GPC, NALT) creates higher energy demands. CoQ10 and NADH ensure adequate ATP production to meet these demands, supporting mental strength during intense cognitive work.**</p><p>Phosphatidylserine maintains membrane fluidity and function, while CoQ10 supports those same membranes from occasional oxidative stress—creating comprehensive membrane support for optimal neural function.**</p>",
            "research_highlights": "Over 7,000 published studies on CoQ10 and human health**\nClinical trials show cognitive support for healthy aging**\nResearch demonstrates support for mitochondrial function and ATP production**\nStudies confirm neuroprotective support against occasional oxidative stress**\nCardiovascular research shows support for heart health and healthy blood pressure**\nMeta-analysis supports use for energy, cognitive function, and longevity**",
            "dosage_info": "",
            "safety_notes": "Backed by thousands of clinical studies on cardiovascular and cognitive health**\nThird-party verified for potency and stability\nWell-tolerated with no major adverse effects at clinical dose"
          }
        },
        "ingredient_PjWV7r": {
          "type": "ingredient",
          "settings": {
            "ingredient_name": "NADH",
            "ingredient_tagline": "THE ENERGY AMPLIFIER**",
            "ingredient_description": "<p>NADH is the reduced form of the coenzyme NAD, which is derived from vitamin B3. NAD and NADH are critical in cellular energy metabolism and help support the body’s natural DNA‑repair processes and healthy aging pathways, mental clarity, stamina, and focus.**</p>",
            "benefits_list": "Mitochondrial Health**\nMental Energy**\nCognitive Clarity**\nFocus & Alertness**\nStamina Support**\nNeurotransmitter Production**\nCellular Vitality**",
            "ingredient_image": "shopify://shop_images/igniton-cognition-nadh.jpg",
            "quantum_enhancement": "Energizes cells, supports cognitive clarity**",
            "anchor_id": "quantum-ingredient",
            "extended_description": "<p>NADH (Nicotinamide Adenine Dinucleotide + Hydrogen) is a coenzyme found in all living cells and plays a vital role in the body’s energy metabolism. It’s the reduced form of NAD⁺, derived from vitamin B3, and is central to the mitochondrial production of ATP—the energy currency of cells. By facilitating redox reactions, NADH helps convert food into usable energy, supporting cellular vitality and metabolic efficiency.**</p><p>Beyond its foundational role in energy, NADH contributes to brain health by supporting neurotransmitter synthesis, particularly dopamine and norepinephrine, which are linked to alertness, motivation, and cognitive function. This makes NADH especially valuable for individuals looking to support mental clarity, focus, and stamina—particularly in high-demand or age-related cognitive contexts. It helps synchronize mental performance with cellular energy.**</p>",
            "how_it_works": "<p>NADH works by acting as a vital electron carrier within your cells: in the reduced form it donates electrons to the mitochondrial electron transport chain, helping to drive ATP production—the energy currency of cells.**</p><p>Because this redox cycling between NADH and its oxidised partner NAD⁺ also influences cellular signalling, mitochondrial health and redox balance, NADH helps support the energetic foundation underlying cognition, focus and vitality.**</p>",
            "formulation_synergy": "<p>NADH works synergistically with the other ingredients in <em>IgniCognition™</em> by providing energetic support to the metabolic foundation of cognitive performance. As a key coenzyme in mitochondrial ATP production, NADH enhances the cellular energy needed for neurotransmitter synthesis and brain signal processing. When combined with nootropic compounds like Citicoline and Alpha-GPC—which help maintain healthy acetylcholine levels—NADH ensures those neurotransmitters are produced and utilized with maximum efficiency. This cellular vitality becomes the energetic groundwork that supports clarity, memory, and mental stamina.**</p><p>Meanwhile, ingredients like N-Acetyl L-Tyrosine support dopamine and norepinephrine pathways for mood and alertness, while CoQ10 and Phosphatidylserine reinforce mitochondrial health and neuroprotection. NADH amplifies the function of these compounds by supporting redox balance and metabolic throughput. Together—especially when enhanced by <em>Igni</em>ton quantum-charging—these ingredients create a coherent, bioenergetically aligned formula that helps synchronize mental clarity, rapid processing, and sustained cognitive resilience.**</p>",
            "research_highlights": "Supports cellular energy metabolism, acting as a coenzyme in ATP production**\nPlays a role in neurotransmitter synthesis, including dopamine and norepinephrine**\nMay improve mental clarity and reduce fatigue, according to clinical research in patients with chronic fatigue and related conditions**\nStudied for cognitive benefits in aging populations and in cases of mild cognitive impairment**\nBacked by decades of biochemical research on NAD/NADH redox cycles and their roles in mitochondrial health**",
            "dosage_info": "",
            "safety_notes": "Third-party tested for purity\nGRAS (Generally Recognized As Safe) status\nNo known serious side effects at recommended doses\nClinically tested for cellular energy and cognitive benefits*"
          }
        }
      },
